      },
      "description": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An interactive globe to explore the future through the places we know.",
          "spans": []
        }
      ],
      "detail_description": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "fromearth / 2050 is a free browser experience for exploring climate projections through the places we know. Search for a city, turn the globe, move from 2026 towards 2050, or compare two places side by side.",
          "spans": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Climate change is often described through global averages and distant horizons. This project begins with somewhere familiar: the city you live in, a place you grew up, somewhere you love. An invitation to explore a complex subject, with access to the sources and definitions behind it.",
          "spans": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The visual language pairs a restrained interface with tactile imagery and motion. Thermal landscapes, layered contours and a graphite Earth extend the experience into a campaign. These illustrations are distinct from the live climate data.",
          "spans": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The four interactive studies above isolate the identity, globe, time control and refracting lens. They give each gesture room to be experienced on its own; climate indicators and comparisons are available on the full website.",
          "spans": []
        }
      ],
